/**
 * Tier-2 `miscellaneous` (+ `settings`-tagged) table-free reads — SPEC-0004
 * appendix A rows served entirely from static vendored data or existing
 * stores, no schema changes. Upstream handlers and their pins:
 *
 *   - gitignore templates: routers/api/v1/misc/gitignore.go:16–46 over
 *     `repo_module.Gitignores` / `options.Gitignore` (modules/repository/
 *     init.go:77–79 LoadRepoConfig sorted listing; modules/options/base.go:36).
 *     The template set is embedded verbatim from the read-only gitea/
 *     submodule's `options/gitignore/` at the pinned commit (270 files) —
 *     Workers cannot read the filesystem, and the wire names must mirror the
 *     pinned set exactly.
 *   - label templates: routers/api/v1/misc/label_templates.go:15–54 over
 *     `LabelTemplateFiles` (init.go:84–103: display name = file name minus
 *     extension, description = the label names joined ", " — parser.go:104–117)
 *     and `LoadTemplateLabelsByDisplayName` (init.go:150–157). The two vendored
 *     templates' PARSED label arrays are embedded (label.LoadTemplateFile,
 *     modules/label/parser.go:37–79 — YAML flavor for Advanced.yaml, legacy
 *     `#color name ; description` flavor for Default, colors through
 *     NormalizeColor).
 *   - license templates: routers/api/v1/misc/licenses.go:24–71 over
 *     `repo_module.Licenses` / `options.License`. The list entry `name`/`key`
 *     is the file name itself and the URL is AppURL + "api/v1/licenses/" +
 *     PathEscape(name) (licenses.go:33–40/60–66). Upstream's
 *     PreferredLicenses promotion (init.go:104–113, default
 *     ["Apache License 2.0", "MIT License"]) matches NO vendored file name, so
 *     the served order is the plain sorted order — verified against the
 *     embedded set.
 *   - POST /markup: routers/api/v1/misc/markup.go Markup (markup.go:25–34)
 *     binding MarkupOption, mode = Iif(Wiki, "wiki", Mode), rendering through
 *     the same common.RenderMarkup port as POST /markdown
 *     (services/markdown.ts, which mirrors markup.go:24–96). The MarkupOption
 *     `FilePath` field ("file mode extension detection", markup.go:14) is
 *     accepted but unused — the landed renderer keys on the mode only.
 *   - GET/DELETE /token: routers/api/v1/token/token.go GetCurrentToken:19–52 /
 *     DeleteCurrentToken:55–73, wired reqToken() (api.go:1036–1038). The
 *     CurrentAccessToken body carries the PRESENTED credential's row
 *     (getToken, token.go:75–84: bearer-token header parse → lookup by SHA).
 *     Runtime-only codes (the /user 401 class, undeclared in the vendored
 *     swagger, NOT added to the orchestrator's RUNTIME_ONLY_RESPONSES table by
 *     this batch): 401 for anonymous/unknown credentials (reqToken), 404 when
 *     the authenticated identity arrived without a token-scheme header (the
 *     getToken ErrNotExist arm, token.go:80–84 — reachable only through the
 *     production `resolveAuth` identity precedence, api/auth.ts identityFrom).
 *   - settings: routers/api/v1/settings/settings.go:14–89 (GetGeneral*
 *     handlers) — anonymous, api.go:1027–1032. Values published:
 *     api = the exact runtime constants our routes enforce
 *     (modules/setting/api.go:17–22 defaults; pagination.ts 30/50,
 *     routes/git.ts trees-per-page 1000 / max blob 10485760);
 *     repository = every feature our instance ships is enabled, time tracking
 *     is honestly advertised DISABLED (no times model — the /user/times and
 *     stopwatch families are unimplemented, upstream default
 *     `EnableTimetracking=true` would be a lie here);
 *     ui = default theme mirrors upstream's default (`gitea-auto`,
 *     modules/setting/ui.go:99), allowed_reactions is the SAME set the
 *     reaction routes enforce (services/issue-extras.ts ALLOWED_REACTIONS ==
 *     ui.go:102 default), custom_emojis is [] (none are served);
 *     attachment = upstream's default allow-list/max-files
 *     (modules/setting/attachment.go:17–21) — neither is enforced by the
 *     release-asset uploads, documented divergence — while max_size publishes
 *     OUR real 413 threshold (512 MiB, services/release-assets.ts:51) instead
 *     of upstream's 100 MB default.
 *
 * DROPPED from the brief's candidate list (with reasons):
 *   - GET /signing-key.gpg + /signing-key.pub (misc/signing.go:14–24): the
 *     only reachable statuses without a configured signing key are 404 ("no
 *     signing key") / 500, but the vendored contract declares 200 ONLY — the
 *     404 cannot be declared (check-openapi subset rule) and cf-gitea has no
 *     signing-key configuration to legitimately answer 200 with. Needs the
 *     orchestrator's RUNTIME_ONLY_RESPONSES entry or a key-config feature
 *     first.
 *   - GET /emoji, /nodeinfo, /.well-known/nodeinfo: NOT PRESENT in the frozen
 *     contract for this submodule pin — a served route without a contract
 *     entry fails check (a).
 *
 * The `{name}` path params go through a PathJoinRelX port
 * (modules/util/path.go:74–83: backslashes→slashes, Clean, empty → ".")
 * before the exact-case map lookup — the embedded names are case-sensitive
 * keys like upstream's asset filesystem.
 */

